  "query_preview": "..Today should be a bit of a down day for convection\nas the activity from Friday has worked over most of the atmosphere.\nShortwave that was the trigger for this event is also departing \nto the east, but still enough left over moisture remains that \ndaytime heating and terrain may trigger a few isolated to \nscattered afternoon storms over the Mogollon Rim and White \nMountains. Isolated areas of flash flooding remain possible as\nheavy rain could fall over areas saturated from yesterday's\nactivity.  \n\nThe story for this week will be a series of shortwaves moving\nthrough the westerlies interacting with monsoon moisture over the\nstate with each wave setting off more showers and thunderstorms.\nThe next such shortwave will arrive on Sunday which will lead to\nan uptick in storm chances area wide. Each shortwave brings extra\nshear to the thunderstorm ingredients which could lead to some\nextra strength, organization and even a few severe cells with \ndamaging winds and larger hail. Will have to evaluate each wave as\nit passes for that potential. Activity may also vary from one\nafternoon to the next depending on how much the atmosphere gets\nworked over from the previous day. At this time this pattern looks\nto hold true for the rest of the week.",
